# per-tag ROM sets from tools/gbuild.sh (one .cof per A10 pad)
build_*/

# ring item: the Jaguar controller is an ORIGINAL model (no disc content),
# so unlike every other *_geom/_atlas blob it ships with the repo.
!ctrl_geom.bin
!ctrl_atlas.bin
mrt_gunanim.h

# Generated by the extractor from the user's disc (this repo ships no game data).
# gym_bear.h/gym_lplanes.h appeared when Lara's Home extraction was revived;
# mrt_sect.bin.prepatch is the boundary-patch backup. All three are rebuilt by
# tools/build_cof.sh, so committing them would ship level data AND go stale.
gym_bear.h
gym_lplanes.h
*.prepatch

# ☠️ DISC-DERIVED CONTENT LIVES IN disc/ AND IS NEVER COMMITTED
# (user's call, 2026-08-19, after 43 MB of it was purged from the public repo)
# Everything under disc/ is transcoded or extracted from the user's own Tomb
# Raider disc: the four FMV clips (Eidos/Core footage), the PS1 loading art,
# and the extractor's level/model/texture output. tools/build_cof.sh and the
# Docker image regenerate all of it from a disc the user supplies - that is the
# whole design, and it is why none of it belongs in the repo.
# Referenced as disc/<name> by mrt_data.S / room0data.S (.incbin) and found by
# #include via -Idisc (Makefile).
/disc/
cobweb/

# ☠☠ BUILD-OUTPUT / MEASUREMENT-ARM DIRECTORIES — DISC-DERIVED, NEVER COMMIT
# Every container run and every A/B arm drops a full SD payload: OPENLARA.elf
# (the linked image, with the disc's level/texture/model data .incbin'd into
# it), CAVSLOAD.DAT / GYMLOAD.DAT (loading art), the .JV clips and MUSIC.PCM.
# `*.cof` and `*.bin` were already ignored; `.elf` and `.DAT` were NOT, so 28
# untracked paths of disc-derived material were sitting one `git add -A` away
# from a PUBLIC repo (2026-09-06). 43 MB of exactly this had to be purged once
# before — see the /disc/ note above.
# ★ Named by PREFIX rather than one-by-one: the next arm will be called
# something nobody has thought of yet, and a rule that needs updating per
# experiment is a rule that fails on the experiment nobody edited it for.
out/
out_*/
arm[0-9]*/
br_*/
wolf_*/
*.elf
*.DAT
*.JV
